1
00:00:00,094 --> 00:00:02,236
QuarantinePay makes agent-assisted
purchases verifiable.

2
00:00:02,236 --> 00:00:05,236
A buyer approves a signed purchase intent.

3
00:00:05,236 --> 00:00:07,379
PayPal places an authorization hold.

4
00:00:07,379 --> 00:00:12,949
Delivery checks then decide whether to
capture the payment or void the hold.

5
00:00:12,949 --> 00:00:16,378
Every step is visible in one command
center.

6
00:00:16,566 --> 00:00:22,639
This assistant runs Qwen three locally on
our thirty-two gigabyte Tesla V one

7
00:00:22,639 --> 00:00:23,107
hundred.

8
00:00:23,107 --> 00:00:26,844
Prompts and product text stay on this
server.

9
00:00:26,844 --> 00:00:31,984
The model can recommend an invoice
artifact, but receives no payment

10
00:00:31,984 --> 00:00:34,319
credentials or authority to spend.

11
00:00:34,319 --> 00:00:37,589
Private mode also searches our local
catalog.

12
00:00:37,589 --> 00:00:42,261
PayPal receives the approved payment
fields required by its API.

13
00:00:42,449 --> 00:00:47,093
Now we change the merchant identifier
after the intent is signed.

14
00:00:47,093 --> 00:00:52,158
The gateway rejects the altered intent
before a PayPal order is created.

15
00:00:52,158 --> 00:00:56,379
The recipient and amount remain bound to
the buyer-approved intent.

16
00:00:56,567 --> 00:00:59,220
First, the failing delivery.

17
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:06,514
QuarantinePay creates a PayPal Sandbox
order and waits for buyer approval.

18
00:01:06,514 --> 00:01:11,156
After approval, the server authorizes one
dollar.

19
00:01:11,156 --> 00:01:13,809
Capture waits for verification.

20
00:01:13,809 --> 00:01:19,114
The invoice then fails its deterministic
arithmetic check.

21
00:01:19,114 --> 00:01:26,409
The worker requests a void using the
stored authorization and request

22
00:01:26,409 --> 00:01:27,072
identifier.

23
00:01:27,072 --> 00:01:35,693
The red timeline and audit event appear
only when PayPal confirms the void.

24
00:01:35,693 --> 00:01:40,999
Signature checks, deadlines, and one-time
nonces remain enforced.

25
00:01:40,999 --> 00:01:46,967
The authorization hold provides a
verification window before settlement.

26
00:01:47,155 --> 00:01:54,442
For a valid delivery, the buyer again
approves the signed transaction and

27
00:01:54,442 --> 00:01:56,871
PayPal authorizes the hold.

28
00:01:56,871 --> 00:02:02,336
This time, the invoice satisfies the
agreed acceptance policy.

29
00:02:02,336 --> 00:02:09,015
Quantities and prices produce the exact
approved total, and the verifier

30
00:02:09,015 --> 00:02:11,445
returns a passing result.

31
00:02:11,445 --> 00:02:16,302
Only then does the worker capture the
authorization.

32
00:02:16,302 --> 00:02:21,160
The timeline turns green after PayPal
confirms completion.

33
00:02:21,160 --> 00:02:26,018
Durable operations, stable request
identifiers, and provider-state checks

34
00:02:26,018 --> 00:02:29,054
support safe recovery after interruptions.

35
00:02:29,054 --> 00:02:35,126
We independently checked the recipient,
amount, and final payment status

36
00:02:35,126 --> 00:02:37,555
against PayPal's own API.

37
00:02:37,744 --> 00:02:41,285
QuarantinePay joins local artificial
intelligence, signed purchase intents,

38
00:02:41,285 --> 00:02:44,382
deterministic delivery checks, and
confirmed PayPal settlement.

39
00:02:44,382 --> 00:02:49,693
It creates a visible, testable boundary
between what an agent recommends and

40
00:02:49,693 --> 00:02:51,906
what the buyer actually approves.

41
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:55,647
We also verified the live
Channel3 path.

42
00:02:55,647 --> 00:02:58,835
The fixed public seed returned
eight listings.

43
00:02:58,835 --> 00:03:02,953
All eight passed local screening,
and none were withheld.

44
00:03:02,953 --> 00:03:07,071
A follow-up search found five
in our local mirror.

45
00:03:07,071 --> 00:03:12,271
These listings are for discovery only
and cannot change checkout.
